WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.268
WIL WILLIS: Gladen,

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:03.669
You guys have made it into
the third and final round

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:05.037
of this competition.

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:06.338
Now it's time to send you
back to your home forges

00:00:06.438 --> 00:00:09.376
to recreate this iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:16.649
The Boateng saber.

00:00:16.715 --> 00:00:19.585
Here to tell you more about
it, historic weapons recreation

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.654
specialist David Baker.

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:23.289
 The Boateng saber
holds the world

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.525
record as the most
expensive sword

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:29.529
ever sold at $7.7 million.

00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:31.664
Commissioned by the
Chinese emperor Qianlong

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:35.735
in the 18th century, this
elaborate weapon is inlaid

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:38.171
with gold, copper, and jewels.

00:00:38.237 --> 00:00:40.874
In addition to its beauty,
the slightly curved blade

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:44.610
featured a sharp, lethal
edge, ideal for slashing

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:46.145
into an opponent.

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:48.114
Combining artisanal
craftsmanship

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:50.383
and deadly practicality,
this weapon

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:52.752
is worthy of an
all-powerful ruler.

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:54.487
 $7.7 million?

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:56.722
Damn, no pressure.

00:00:56.822 --> 00:00:57.723
 Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:59.558
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:00.326
 Good luck.

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:03.095 line:7%
 Good luck.

00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:04.464
It's the morning of day two.

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:05.565
I'm feeling pretty good.

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:06.699
A little sleepy.

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:09.035
My main goal today is to
get it all ground down,

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:11.337
get the fullers in, and clinch.

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.039 line:0%
I want a really
big fuller in it,

00:01:13.105 --> 00:01:16.276 line:0%
just so it knocks a
lot of the weight out.

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:18.945
Now I'm going to go
to the heat treat.

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:22.114
I really hope this
fits in there.

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:23.483
I don't know if it
got hard or not.

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:27.720
It's not really getting hard.

00:01:27.821 --> 00:01:29.556
There's a couple
dead spots in it.

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:32.158
I think I'm just going to have
to redo the quench because I

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:33.693
don't want to risk
having, you know,

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:37.863
a super bent blade on
any of the tests they do.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:38.598
Here we go.

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:46.139
[rock music]

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:47.340
Looks pretty good.

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:55.448
MATT: [groans] Starting day two.

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:57.883
What I want to
get done is finish

00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:59.252
the profile of the saber.

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:05.224
Because I'm forging,
the exhaustion

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:07.193
just starts to set in.

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:09.762
I'd pay $700 for a
Big Blue right now.

00:02:09.828 --> 00:02:15.167
[chuckles] It's starting to
look like a Boateng saber now.

00:02:15.267 --> 00:02:17.870
 It's the morning of day three.

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:20.439
But I still have
got a lot to do.

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:22.575
The handle tier is moving
really, really slow.

00:02:22.641 --> 00:02:25.044
And I've already clogged
up about four belts.

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:29.281
And I've got to save some
for the blade finishing.

00:02:29.381 --> 00:02:31.851
I'm going to start getting a
little bit nicer of a profile

00:02:31.917 --> 00:02:34.153
and just start cleaning it up.

00:02:34.219 --> 00:02:37.189
So I pretty much
finished up the blade.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.225
It's been a pretty
tough challenge.

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:40.526
I'm extremely tired.

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:42.494
My back is killing me
from all the grinding.

00:02:42.561 --> 00:02:44.463
But tomorrow's the
last day, and I'm going

00:02:44.563 --> 00:02:46.131
to turn in an amazing weapon.

00:02:46.231 --> 00:02:49.702
[blows raspberry]

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:51.003
 It's day four.

00:02:51.069 --> 00:02:52.639
I've got a torch and a sword.

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:53.939
Get out of my way.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.775
Yesterday, we got
the quench done.

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:58.110
And it went awesome.

00:02:58.177 --> 00:02:59.078
It's still hard.

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:00.213
So that's good.

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:01.814
I've got a piece of brass stock.

00:03:01.914 --> 00:03:03.148
This will make a nice guard.

00:03:03.215 --> 00:03:06.752
[chuckles] Almost there.

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:08.154
I find a piece of walnut.

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:09.388
It's dark.

00:03:09.488 --> 00:03:12.858
So I think it'll look
cool with the brass.

00:03:12.925 --> 00:03:14.594
I just gotta cut it in half.

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:20.967
Ow!

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:25.672
[bleep] [groans]

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:27.874
It went through there quicker
than I thought it would.

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:31.911
[laughs] I ain't
got time to bleed.

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:33.779
Let's go.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.048
We'd better clean it up,
wrap some tape around it,

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:38.517
and keep going.

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.419
I'm really worried
at this point.

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:42.088
Am I going to lose time?

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:43.756
Am I going to be able
to finish this sword?

00:03:48.927 --> 00:03:52.231
All bandaged up and ready to go.

00:03:52.331 --> 00:03:54.032
Let's get back to work.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.234
I'll make it.

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:56.502
It ain't going to stop me.

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:58.170
But I really have
to take my time,

00:03:58.237 --> 00:04:01.206
be careful, and
not be in a hurry.

00:04:01.273 --> 00:04:05.844
Let that be a
lesson to everybody.

00:04:05.944 --> 00:04:06.646
The final stretch.

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:11.784
My Boateng saber
is made of sweat,

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:13.286
rain, and blood, literally.

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:16.823
[chuckles] I got an
emperor to deliver this to.

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:17.590
Gotta go.

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:24.464
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the KEAL test.

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:25.932
To find out how lethal
weapon your weapons are,

00:04:25.998 --> 00:04:28.367
we'll take your weapons to
deliver some lethal blows

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.369
on this boar carcass.

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:32.504
It's time to find out if
your blades will stand up

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:35.275
to the most expensive
blade ever sold in auction

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:37.243
or if they're going on a
"Forged in Fire" reduced sale.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:38.977
[laughter]

00:04:39.044 --> 00:04:39.812
Gladen, you're up first.

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:40.579
You ready for this?

00:04:40.679 --> 00:04:42.982
 Yes, I am.

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:44.950
[rock music]

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:49.956
[impact sounds]

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:05.838
 All right, Gladen, let's
talk about your weapon here.

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:07.273
You're extra sharp.

00:05:07.339 --> 00:05:08.908
That's a thick hide right there.

00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:10.710
And it chops deep into it.

00:05:10.776 --> 00:05:14.680
Overall, sir, your
Boateng will KEAL.

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:15.648
 OK.

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:16.749
 All right, Matt,
your turn, sir.

00:05:16.816 --> 00:05:17.616
Are you ready?

00:05:17.683 --> 00:05:20.987
 Let's bring home the bacon.

00:05:21.054 --> 00:05:26.459
[impact sounds]

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:36.703
 Good job, dude.

00:05:39.604 --> 00:05:41.007
DOUG MARCAIDA: All right, Matt.

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:42.742
I like the bounce that you
have with your weapon here.

00:05:42.809 --> 00:05:45.010
Your handle is a
little bit blocky.

00:05:45.077 --> 00:05:47.280
So when you have a blocky
handle right there, when you're

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:50.282
swinging for the rafters
right there with full power,

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:51.651
it tends to move around.

00:05:51.717 --> 00:05:53.820
I can't get full grip on this.

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:55.621
Your edge is sharp though.

00:05:55.721 --> 00:05:58.624
Some of the chops
there, it goes deep.

00:05:58.725 --> 00:05:59.658
It will KEAL.

00:05:59.758 --> 00:06:00.792
 Thank you.

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:03.996
 Bladesmiths, welcome to
one of my favorite tests,

00:06:04.096 --> 00:06:07.265
the ice block chop, supersized.

00:06:07.366 --> 00:06:08.501
Now, I'm going to
take your swords

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:10.402
and beat them repeatedly
and mercilessly

00:06:10.502 --> 00:06:12.571
into this large block of ice.

00:06:12.638 --> 00:06:16.008
A good, strong sword should be
able to hold up to the stress.

00:06:16.109 --> 00:06:17.943
One that's not so
good might chip,

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:20.412
bend, or even break apart.

00:06:20.512 --> 00:06:22.047
Gladen, how you feeling, buddy?

00:06:22.114 --> 00:06:22.782
 A little nauseous.

00:06:26.152 --> 00:06:29.655
 [grunts]

00:06:46.138 --> 00:06:47.439
 All right, Gladen, nice job.

00:06:47.506 --> 00:06:49.408
A little bit forward-heavy.

00:06:49.508 --> 00:06:51.143
But good, strong blade.

00:06:51.243 --> 00:06:52.411
Your edge is perfect.

00:06:52.511 --> 00:06:54.113
No damage at all.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.248
Good job.

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:58.117
How are you feeling, Matt?

00:06:58.184 --> 00:06:59.918
 After watching
that, I don't know.

00:06:59.985 --> 00:07:00.719
[laughs]

00:07:00.819 --> 00:07:01.821
 Well, we're going to find out.

00:07:12.198 --> 00:07:15.668
 [grunts]

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:21.073
 Nice.

00:07:25.944 --> 00:07:27.413
J. NEILSON: All right,
Matt, you survived.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.514
Everything's still tight.

00:07:28.581 --> 00:07:30.549
Nothing came loose.

00:07:30.649 --> 00:07:35.587
But your edge is
not what it was.

00:07:35.654 --> 00:07:38.224
It hasn't exactly
rolled over or chipped.

00:07:38.324 --> 00:07:40.492
It just doesn't
have that razor edge

00:07:40.559 --> 00:07:42.361
it did have when I started.

00:07:42.461 --> 00:07:43.829
But hey, man, you survived.

00:07:43.896 --> 00:07:44.363
Good job.

00:07:44.463 --> 00:07:45.731
 Thank you.

00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:47.366
 All right, bladesmiths,
welcome to the sharpest

00:07:47.433 --> 00:07:50.369
test, the tatami mat slice.

00:07:50.435 --> 00:07:52.605
Now, we'll take your
weapon and try to cut

00:07:52.705 --> 00:07:54.307
through these tatami mats.

00:07:54.373 --> 00:07:56.675
A sharp blade should
cut all the way through.

00:07:56.742 --> 00:07:57.710
Gladen, you're up first.

00:07:57.777 --> 00:07:58.310
You ready?

00:07:58.377 --> 00:07:59.245
 Yes, sir.

00:07:59.312 --> 00:07:59.979
 Let's do it.

00:08:04.517 --> 00:08:10.490
[impact sounds]

00:08:18.197 --> 00:08:19.464
Cha-ching!

00:08:19.564 --> 00:08:20.466
All right, Gladen.

00:08:20.532 --> 00:08:22.033
Let's talk about your edge here.

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:23.269
It's sharp.

00:08:23.336 --> 00:08:24.703
It cut through the
first three tatamis

00:08:24.803 --> 00:08:26.772
easily, even on the
one that's doubled up.

00:08:26.839 --> 00:08:30.209
Overall, sir, your
weapon, it will cut.

00:08:30.276 --> 00:08:31.810
 Thank you, sir.

00:08:31.911 --> 00:08:33.145
 All right, Matt,
your turn, sir.

00:08:33.212 --> 00:08:33.912
You ready?

00:08:34.013 --> 00:08:34.747
 Let's do it.

00:08:34.813 --> 00:08:36.015
DOUG MARCAIDA: Let's do this.

00:08:36.082 --> 00:08:40.586
[impact sounds]

00:08:50.429 --> 00:08:51.663
All right, Matt.

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:53.799
As you can see, it
did cut a little bit.

00:08:53.865 --> 00:08:56.335
But during the strength test,
it did get some dulling.

00:08:56.402 --> 00:08:58.938
It's still sharp, but
it's not as sharp.

00:08:59.005 --> 00:09:01.340
But this is the reason why
we have the sharpness test,

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:04.143
so we know how well your
edge is able to hold

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:05.478
on to its sharpness.

00:09:05.578 --> 00:09:09.481
But you can see, in the
first cuts, it will cut.

00:09:09.548 --> 00:09:11.383
 Thank you.

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:12.651
 All right,
gentlemen, the judges

00:09:12.717 --> 00:09:13.819
have made their final decision.

00:09:13.919 --> 00:09:18.090
Our new "Forged in
Fire" champion is--

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:19.659
Gladen.

00:09:19.759 --> 00:09:21.059
Congratulations, you're the
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:21.159 --> 00:09:23.896
Matt, unfortunately, your
blade didn't make the cut.

00:09:23.996 --> 00:09:26.031
Matt, you did fantastic
work, but at this time,

00:09:26.131 --> 00:09:28.934
I'm going to have to ask
you to exit the forge.

00:09:29.001 --> 00:09:29.568
Good job.

00:09:29.668 --> 00:09:30.269
 Thanks very much.

00:09:30.369 --> 00:09:31.737
 Good job.

00:09:31.803 --> 00:09:32.971
MATT: Oh, just a little bummed.

00:09:33.038 --> 00:09:34.940
Overall, I feel like
I made a good sword.

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:39.612
It survived chopping a big block
of ice, so that's pretty good.

00:09:39.678 --> 00:09:40.579
I'm proud of that.

00:09:40.679 --> 00:09:41.914
Congratulations, man.

00:09:42.014 --> 00:09:44.683
"Forged in Fire" is a
really tough challenge.

00:09:44.783 --> 00:09:49.621
It really pushes you to
really expand on your skills.

00:09:49.688 --> 00:09:51.756
 Gladen, you are the
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:51.857 --> 00:09:53.359
That's a title
that does not come

00:09:53.459 --> 00:09:55.561
with a check for
$7.7 million, but it

00:09:55.627 --> 00:09:57.630
does come with one for $10,000.

00:09:57.696 --> 00:09:58.497
Good job, brother.

00:09:58.564 --> 00:09:59.231
[applause]

00:09:59.331 --> 00:10:01.233
 Thank you.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:03.268
WIL WILLIS: Come over
here and shake our hand.

00:10:03.335 --> 00:10:04.136
 Thank you.

00:10:04.203 --> 00:10:05.004
 Good job, brother.

00:10:05.071 --> 00:10:06.105
You did a great job.

00:10:06.171 --> 00:10:07.539
MAN: The whole "Forged
in Fire" experience

00:10:07.639 --> 00:10:09.174
has been fantastic for
me, all the learning

00:10:09.241 --> 00:10:10.843
that I've been able to do.

00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:11.643
 Nice job.

00:10:11.743 --> 00:10:12.511
Just a little lighter next time.

00:10:12.578 --> 00:10:13.812
 I know.

00:10:13.912 --> 00:10:15.014
Being the "Forged in
Fire" champion gives me

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:16.548
the confirmation
that, you know, I can

00:10:16.615 --> 00:10:18.551
make good swords and blades.

00:10:18.651 --> 00:10:20.519
It tells me I'm going
in the right direction.

00:10:20.619 --> 00:10:22.454
So it should be 7.7 million.

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:23.822
But you know, I'll take 10,000.

00:10:23.889 --> 00:10:24.390
Woo!

00:10:24.457 --> 00:10:27.827
[music playing]

